# This root-level file is a reference index only — it is not read by any
# tool directly. Each runnable project has its own .env.example that you
# actually copy from:
#
#   web/.env.example      -> copy to web/.env.local
#   backend/.env.example  -> copy to backend/.env (or backend/.env.local)
#
# See ENVIRONMENT.md for what each variable means, which phase introduces
# it, and where its real value will come from (e.g., a Supabase project's
# settings page, or the Google Cloud Console OAuth client). Never commit a
# filled-in .env/.env.local file, and never hardcode a secret anywhere in
# source (SECURITY_ARCHITECTURE.md §10).
